Ah; some source diving shows that the symbols you mention only get used if
certain compile time options (e.g. MSDOS) are defined, whereas the 
monsyms[S_HUMAN] = 0x01;
line gets called even if MSDOS is not defined.

I didn't find anything definitive, but it looks to me like anything under
0x20 should be considered unprintable, and that that's what most unix
terminals are now doing.

